# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.
ignoreInGit
# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# Every alternate build directory, as one pattern.
#
# There are five of them and there keeps being another: `.next-shots` and
# `.next-shots2` for the screenshot servers, `.next-build` and `.next-verify`
# for production builds that must not stomp on `.next` (which the dev server
# owns), `.next-classname` for the CSS-attribute build whose chunks must never
# be picked up by a normal dev server. Each was listed by hand, so each new one
# was committed by accident once first.
#
# `.next` itself is `/.next/` further down, and `next-env.d.ts` does not start
# with a dot, so neither is caught by this.
.next-*
.shoot-profile
# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# The event agent's public key, pasted out of the app box so it can be added to
# the Hetzner project. Only the public half is ever written here - the private
# key stays on the box that generated it and is never copied anywhere. Ignored
# because it is a per-install fact about one machine, not part of the source.
*.pub.local

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Production data dumped for the local stack (bun run db:dump-prod).
# Real emails and password hashes - never commit this.
supabase/seed.sql

# Post-ready renders, rebuilt from the scenes by `bun run scripts/build-social.ts`.
# Ten megabytes of PNG that is a pure function of files already in the repo -
# the plan and the copy next to them are the part worth keeping. `public/og.png`
# comes out of the same script and *is* committed: it ships with the site.
docs/marketing/images/

# eslint --cache, written by deploy.sh
.eslintcache

# Worktrees an agent session created. Never committed: each one is a full
# checkout of this repo, and a stray `git add -A` would try to commit all of it.
.claude/worktrees/

# Playwright's own output. The specs are checked in; their traces are not.
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# Recordings from `VIDEO=1`. Watched, not committed.
/e2e/video/

# The camera-original screen recordings behind `public/enter/introduction-*.mp4`.
# Forty-four megabytes for ninety seconds, and the file that ships is a tenth of
# that with no visible difference (see `bun run scripts/…`, or the ffmpeg line in
# docs). Kept on disk so the shipped one can be re-encoded from the original
# rather than from an already-compressed copy; never committed, because a repo
# that carries both is carrying the same ninety seconds twice.
/public/enter/*.source.*

# Published from packages/boxing/assets by `bun run boxing:assets --publish`.
# The package is the source; this is a build output.
/public/boxing

# ...and the same for the card game. `bun run maumau:assets --publish`.
/public/maumau
